## Experience Philosophy

Experience is not visual design.

Experience is professional behaviour.

Every interaction should help operators answer one or more institutional questions.

Examples include:

What changed?

Why did it change?

What is affected?

What requires my attention?

What should I investigate?

What decision is required?

What action is appropriate?

What happened after execution?

The Experience Architecture therefore organises interactions around professional reasoning rather than software functionality.



